# Desktop-first UI assumptions

Unless the user explicitly mentions **mobile**, **phone**, **tablet**, **touch**, or similar (e.g. "mobile version"), assume they mean the **PC / desktop** experience.

## When implementing UI changes

- Prioritize desktop viewport, layout, spacing, and hover interactions.
- Do not default to mobile breakpoints, touch targets, or mobile-only reflows unless asked.
- If a change affects both, implement and verify **desktop first**; only adjust mobile when the user requests it or when a desktop fix clearly breaks small screens.

## Examples

- "Make the read message popup wider" → widen the desktop popup; do not treat this as a mobile-only task.
- "Fix the nav on mobile" → apply mobile-specific styles and breakpoints.
